      "writtenOn": "2022-12-16T05:37:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "After checking again I found I was wrong at least about the device I was referring to: HM1100 indeed only runs HFP and controls via AT commands alone. Thus I\u0027ll take the advice to connect only after A2DP.\n\nAfter experimenting with the \"popular\" headsets that we never tried, I found a few more strange behaviors (e.g., some claim AVRCP but never successfully connects \u003d\u003e makes retry-loop/disconnect-on-missing infeasible) and am hesitant to make greater changes before ensuring all of them on our hands work in an expected way.\n\nIMO deferring AVRCP to after A2DP is not a large change and could mitigate a subset of issues so it may be worth landing first.",
      "parentUuid": "04d10773_3f491cac",
